      {
        "number": 8,
        "internalPageId": null,
        "title": "Affirmative Interrogative Negative 1 I have been in Europe for 2 weeks. How long have you been in Europe? I have not been in Europe for 2 weeks. 2 She has won many awards so far. Has she ever won any awards? She, hasn’t won any awards yet. 3 They have stayed in many lodges around the world. Have they stayed in many lodges around the world? They haven’t stayed in many lodges around the world. There are also some adverbs that work with this structure 4 I have already been here for 6 hours. She has just entered the hotel. You have not called them yet.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "Affirmative Interrogative Negative 1 I have been in Europe for 2 weeks. How long have you been in Europe? I have not been in Europe for 2 weeks. 2 She has won many awards so far. Has she ever won any awards? She, hasn’t won any awards yet. 3 They have stayed in many lodges around the world. Have they stayed in many lodges around the world? They haven’t stayed in many lodges around the world. There are also some adverbs that work with this structure 4 I have already been here for 6 hours. She has just entered the hotel. You have not called them yet.",
          "We use present perfect tense to talk about actions that started in the past and have not finished yet."
        ],
        "links": [],
        "media": [
