      {
        "number": 9,
        "internalPageId": null,
        "title": "To Consider 1. Already – used to determine longer periods of time in actions. 2. Just – Used to determine shorter periods of time in actions. 3. Yet –Used to state an actions has not occurred. 4. ALL of them can be in questions and sentences (yet only in questions and negative ones) 5. Have/Has are the auxiliaries. Main verbs must be in past participle. 6. There is a progressive tense that can be used here. E.G I have been waiting for the bus for two hours",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "To Consider 1. Already – used to determine longer periods of time in actions. 2. Just – Used to determine shorter periods of time in actions. 3. Yet –Used to state an actions has not occurred. 4. ALL of them can be in questions and sentences (yet only in questions and negative ones) 5. Have/Has are the auxiliaries. Main verbs must be in past participle. 6. There is a progressive tense that can be used here. E.G I have been waiting for the bus for two hours"
        ],
        "links": [],
