      {
        "number": 11,
        "internalPageId": null,
        "title": "We can use present perfect tense to communicate different functions. Check out the following examples.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "We can use present perfect tense to communicate different functions. Check out the following examples.",
          "Functions Examples 1 Express actions that started in the past and still continue. They have visited us for two weeks already. You have been tall since you were a child. 2 Talk about actions than happened only once or certain times. He has just been there once. We have stayed at your place many times. 3 State unfinished actions We have been expecting him to change for so long. 4 Point out finished actions -Why are you so tired? -I’ve been getting ready for the test all week."
        ],
        "links": [],
        "media": [
          {
            "url": "https://docs.google.com/slides-images-rt/AE1YXSa8Q791zfwvlRE9qqgpHC6Kqy0-Xpi6Mslt07VKeyDu_Vfy9Dae59pK4QJfMOJTREq8D8W7dqZh_39y99M6XGCGjNDPlQxAGOuygFymJbjDwsMG7SYLXxnQ-FPe1CC1YsO2qt3x06OgQGUzhScoi-Z7m0qqeiZWZ3te-J0TgIlHe1nhv7-iyiQ=s2048",
